  "summary": "The commit adds `Parameter.spec` and `Argument.spec`, deprecates `human_readable_name` (it now warns, and so does any subclass that overrides it), and adds `get_help_spec`. It also switches the error hints, the deprecation messages and the deprecated+required check over to `spec`. I picked 39 tests (budget 40). They cover the deprecation tests in test_deprecations, the test_spec and test_spec_and_help_spec tests named after the new property, the help-record tests, and the deprecated_required / deprecated_warning tests that hit the changed messages. I added a few error-hint tests (formatting usage errors, nargs and missing-option errors) for the `get_error_hint` paths.",
